  "entries": {
    "bake": {
      "word": "BAKE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To prepare, as food, by cooking in a dry heat, either in an oven or under coals, or on heated stone or metal; as, to bake bread, meat, apples. which exhausts the moisture in food more than roasting or broiling; but the distinction of meaning between roasting and baking is not always observed.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To dry or harden (anything) by subjecting to heat, as, to bake bricks; the sun bakes the ground.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To harden by cold. The earth . . . is baked with frost. Shak. They bake their sides upon the cold, hard stone. Spenser.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To do the work of baking something; as, she brews, washes, and bakes. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To be baked; to become dry and hard in heat; as, the bread bakes; the ground bakes in the hot sun.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "The process, or result, of baking.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
